##DESCRIPTION
## Calculate the margin of error and confidence interval using the sample proportion
## and confindence inter length. 
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##Tagged by up2p

## DBsubject(Statistics)
## DBchapter(Confidence intervals)
## DBsection(Concepts)
## Institution(ASU)
## Level(3)
## KEYWORDS('confidence interval','margin of error')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

$length = random(0.05, 0.3, 0.01);
$mean   = random(0.3,  0.7, 0.01);

Context('Interval');
$conf_int = Interval($mean - 0.5 * $length, $mean + 0.5 * $length);

BEGIN_PGML
A confidence interval for a population proportion has length [$length].

a)  Determine the margin of error.  [_]{Real(0.5*$length)}

b) If the sample proportion is [$mean], obtain the confidence interval. 

    Confidence interval: [_]{$conf_int}{10}

[@ helpLink('interval') @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a) The margin of error is just half of the length of confidence interval.  In this case it is [$length*0.5].

b) For this case, the center of the interval is the mean or [$mean] and then the endpoints of the interval are the margin of error on either side. 

[```
\begin{aligned}
p_1 & = \hat{p} - \frac{[$length]}{2} = [@ ($conf_int->value)[0]@] &  
p_2 & = \hat{p} + \frac{[$length]}{2}  = [@ ($conf_int->value)[1]@] 
\end{aligned}```]
and therefore the interval is [`[$conf_int]`].
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();       # This should be the last executable line in the problem.